for slug,title,body in [('privacy','Privacy','''<h2>Your inputs stay in this browser.</h2><p>ParseCove’s conversion code processes your text and files on your device. It does not upload tool inputs, use external conversion APIs, save input history, or include advertising, analytics or session-replay scripts.</p><h2>What the hosting platform handles</h2><p>Loading this website sends normal web requests to its hosting provider. The provider may process request metadata, logs and authentication cookies under its own policies. Local processing does not mean visiting the website creates no network requests.</p><h2>Files and clipboard</h2><p>Files are read only when you select or drop them. The clipboard is written only when you press a Copy button. Downloads are created locally. Reloading clears the application’s in-memory inputs; browser form restoration may behave differently.</p><h2>Sharing</h2><p>Tool inputs are not added to the address bar. Downloaded files and anything you copy may still contain personal data; share them thoughtfully.</p>'''),('about','About & methods','''<h2>A small toolbox for everyday work.</h2><p>ParseCove brings everyday developer utilities into one place: Unix timestamp conversion, CSS PX/REM and HEX color conversion, Base64 and HEX text encoding, JSON string escaping, a URL-safe Base64URL tool with hex output, and separate entry points for image encoding and decoding.</p><h2>How calculations work</h2><p>Time inputs are validated before conversion. Whole timestamps are parsed with integer arithmetic and displayed with JavaScript Date and Intl. Base64 follows the standard and URL-safe alphabets in RFC 4648. Text is interpreted as UTF-8. Images are inspected by byte signatures and decoded by your browser. PX/REM conversion uses an explicit root font size and selected rounding precision.</p><h2>Limits are part of the result.</h2><p>Each tool explains its assumptions and restrictions. Timestamp auto-detection is a heuristic. Timezone results depend on your browser’s timezone database. Image preview supports PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP up to 10 MB. CSS conversion uses standard JavaScript numbers and supports numeric values, not whole stylesheets.</p><h2>Free, focused and local.</h2><p>No account is required by the tools. The app has no paid features, input uploads, or third-party analytics. You can inspect the <a href="https://github.com/joshua880604-web/parsecove">source code and conversion tests on GitHub</a>.</p>''')]:
 (D/slug).mkdir(exist_ok=True);(D/slug/'index.html').write_text(layout(slug,title,f'{title} and local processing at ParseCove.',tool_head('', 'PARSECOVE',title,'A little transparency goes a long way.')+'<article class="prose">'+body+'</article>'))
